  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the maintainer (ezzz) who owns the release, I want to give the operator access to the HFR+ app in App Store Connect, so that he can set up signing and an automatic TestFlight pipeline (Xcode Cloud) for SwiftHFR without my having to learn how. This is the first prerequisite of LOT-161 (#251).\n\n### Why\n\n- By the operator's decision of 2026-11-07, ezzz owns the release: version/build numbering (option A: continue the legacy counter, 5.0 (37) or higher, +1 per upload), the App Store Connect key, signing and uploads.\n- ezzz has a paid Apple developer account but has not set up a pipeline. The operator has already set one up on another app:\n  - Xcode Cloud archives and signs the app, then uploads it to TestFlight (internal group, automatic distribution) on a push to a release branch;\n  - Apple holds the distribution certificate and profiles, so there are none in GitHub;\n  - an optional GitHub Action submits to the App Store with an App Store Connect API key kept in GitHub secrets.\n\n### What ezzz does (once, about 5 minutes)\n\n1. App Store Connect → **Users and Access** → **+** → the operator's Apple ID e-mail. This is sent to ezzz privately, never posted here.\n2. Role: **Admin**. Admin includes *Certificates, Identifiers & Profiles* on an organisation team, and only Account Holder or Admin can create App Store provisioning profiles. The minimum alternative is **App Manager**, which can configure Xcode Cloud but cannot create distribution profiles. In that case, ezzz keeps that step.\n3. App access: the HFR+ app, or all apps.\n4. The operator accepts the invitation.\n\nApple references:\n- [Add and edit users](https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-your-team/add-and-edit-users/)\n- [Role permissions](https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/account-management/role-permissions/)\n- [Get started with Xcode Cloud](https://developer.apple.com/xcode-cloud/get-started/)\n- [Create an App Store provisioning profile](https://developer.apple.com/help/account/provisioning-profiles/create-an-app-store-provisioning-profile/)\n\n### What ezzz decides (the operator brings these questions)\n\n- Does SwiftHFR ship as a **new version of the existing HFR+ app** (same bundle ID, TestFlight testers kept) or as a new app record? Option A of 2026-11-07, which continues the legacy build counter, implies the existing app.\n- Who is in the TestFlight internal group (ezzz, the operator, the beta testers)?\n\n### Then (operator, on LOT-161 #251)\n\n- Xcode Cloud workflow « TestFlight (beta) »: archive the `SwiftHFR` scheme, App Store Connect distribution, internal group with automatic distribution.\n- `App/Config/Secrets.xcconfig` keys for the Xcode Cloud build (rehost and Giphy, #555): set as Xcode Cloud environment secrets, never in the repository.\n- A dry run documented on LOT-161 before any real upload (an operator-confirmed action, AGENTS §0).\n\n### Blocked by\n\n- ezzz's App Store Connect invitation (third party; the operator asks him by HFR private message)\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
